 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value that a JSON Pointer
+refers to. `""` is the whole document; `~1` and `~0` escape `/` and `~`. It throws an `Error` when the
+pointer is invalid (not empty and not starting with `/`, or a bad `~` escape) or does not resolve (missing
+member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index, `-`, or descent into a primitive). Run tests with `npm test`.
